{{also|Vibrato}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{etyl|it|en}} ''vibrato'', past participle of ''vibrare'' meaning "to vibrate" or "to quiver"

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɒtəʊ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|music|lang=en}} The musical effect or technique where the pitch or frequency of a note or sound is quickly and repeatedly raised and lowered over a small distance for the duration of that note or sound.

